            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+cohomology"} elliptic cohomology
            one assigns to every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+curve"} elliptic curve
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ϕ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi
            over a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring"} ring
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology+theory"} cohomology theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Brown+representability+theorem"} represented
            by an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/E-%E2%88%9E+ring"} E-∞ ring
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectrum"} spectrum
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mi ϕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_\phi
          %p
            Since, by definition, we may identify the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+curve"} elliptic curve
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ϕ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi
            over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            with a patch
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ϕ
                  %mo :
                  %mi Spec
                  %mi R
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi ℳ
                    %mrow
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi : Spec R \to \mathcal{M}_{1,1}
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+stack"} moduli stack
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ℳ
                    %mrow
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}_{1,1}
            of elliptic curves, this assignment
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝒪
                    %mi Der
                  %mo :
                  %mi ϕ
                  %mo ↦
                  %msub
                    %mi E
                    %mi ϕ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathcal{O}^{Der} : \phi \mapsto E_\phi
          %p
            looks like an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/E-%E2%88%9E+ring"} E-∞ ring
            valued
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structure+sheaf"} structure sheaf
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ℳ
                      %mrow
                        %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}_{1,1}
          %p
            There is a very general theory of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+geometry"} higher geometry
            for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+scheme"} generalized spaces
            with generalized
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structure+sheaf"} structure sheaves
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi ℳ
                    %mrow
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝒪
                    %mi Der
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (\mathcal{M}_{1,1}, \mathcal{O}^{Der})
          %p
            as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structured+%28infinity%2C1%29-topos"} structured space
            that is a “derived”
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Deligne-Mumford+stack"} Deligne-Mumford stack
          %p
            The central theorem about
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+cohomology"} elliptic cohomology
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacob+Lurie"} Jacob Lurie
          .standout
            %p
              %strong the central theorem, first version
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+stack"} moduli stack
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ℳ
                      %mrow
                        %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}_{1,1}
              of
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+curve"} elliptic curve
              = succeed "-valued" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/E-%E2%88%9E+ring"} E-∞ ring
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structure+sheaf"} structure sheaf
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝒪
                      %mi Der
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}^{Der}
              may be regarded as the
              %em derived moduli stack
              of
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+elliptic+curve"} derived elliptic curve
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/E-%E2%88%9E+ring"} E-∞ ring
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              the space of derived stack morphisms
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
